Terminal text editor with an IRC-style interface. Download **one** file for your system; each includes the manual.

| System | Installer | Portable |
|---|---|---|
| Windows 10/11 (64-bit) | `text_killer-@VERSION@-windows-x86_64-setup.exe` (or the `-setup.zip`) | `text_killer-@VERSION@-windows-x86_64.zip` |
| macOS (Apple Silicon and Intel) | `text_killer-@VERSION@-macos-installer.zip` | `text_killer-@VERSION@-macos-apple-silicon.zip` / `text_killer-@VERSION@-macos-intel.zip` |
| Debian / Ubuntu / Mint | `text-killer_@VERSION@_amd64.deb` (`_arm64.deb` for ARM) | `text_killer-@VERSION@-linux-x86_64.tar.gz` |
| Fedora / openSUSE | `text_killer-@VERSION@-1.x86_64.rpm` (`.aarch64.rpm` for ARM) | `text_killer-@VERSION@-linux-x86_64.tar.gz` |
| Arch / Manjaro | `text_killer-bin-@VERSION@-1-x86_64.pkg.tar.zst` (`-aarch64` for ARM; or build with `PKGBUILD`) | `text_killer-@VERSION@-linux-x86_64.tar.gz` |
| Any other Linux | `text_killer-@VERSION@-linux-x86_64.tar.gz`, then `./install.sh` | same file |

Arch: `sudo pacman -U text_killer-bin-@VERSION@-1-x86_64.pkg.tar.zst`
Debian/Ubuntu: `sudo apt install ./text-killer_@VERSION@_amd64.deb`
Fedora: `sudo dnf install ./text_killer-@VERSION@-1.x86_64.rpm`

The Linux programs are statically linked and need no libraries.

